// The Last Morning — yuddha kanda, Lanka
// Source: Uttara Kanda, Uttara Kanda, sargas 10, 16 (verify) (later tradition)
// Migrated from the old script format. Not yet staged for the Ramlila stage.

>> scene lankaNight style=kachni
>> music lanka
>> cast ravana at 0.4
>> title Meanwhile, in Lanka / The Last Morning
Before dawn. His brother is dead, and his sons. The streets are full of widows. He is alone in a palace of gold.
>> scene hermitage clear
>> prop fire fireRite at 0.6 state=0.6
>> enter ravana from left to 0.4 in 0.1
>> set ravana pose=kneel
He remembers. Ten thousand years of austerity, when he was young. At the end of each thousand he offered one of his heads to the fire, like a lotus. He was reaching for the tenth when Brahma came.
_: Ask.
RAVANA: Let me not be killed by gods, or demons, or serpents, or spirits, or any of the great ones.
Men he did not mention. It did not occur to him that a man could matter.
>> scene kailash clear
>> enter ravana from left to 0.46 in 0.1
>> set ravana pose=grieve
He remembers Kailash. He tried to lift Shiva's mountain out of his way, and Shiva pressed down one toe, and he was pinned. He screamed, and then, because he was what he was, he began to sing.
He sang for a thousand years, until he was forgiven, and given a sword, and a name: Ravana, the one who roars.
>> scene lankaNight clear
>> enter ravana from left to 0.4 in 0.1
>> set ravana pose=stand
The heads speak for the last time.
>> heads \{"silent":"l6.silent","lines":\{"scholar":"l6.12","devotee":"l6.13","brother":"l6.14","father":"l6.15","honour":"l6.16","fear":"l6.17","anger":"l6.18","desire":"l6.19","pride":"l6.20","king":"l6.21"\}\}
>> enter mandodari from right to 0.66 in 1.4
MANDODARI: Send her back. I am asking for the last time. I have asked every night.
>> move ravana to 0.56 in 1.2
>> pose ravana give
He kisses her forehead. He does not answer. There is nothing new to say.
>> exit ravana to left in 2
He goes down to his chariot.
-> END
